9797 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "60baa69f-bbf2-5905-831d-ab5e879fa2f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389797 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0,0.5]\\times [0,1]={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,0.5],b\\in [0,1]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(0.5,0),$ $(0.5,1),$ and $(0,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/5b/5b882f3fb0e7b44eb2df3a510260574e5c4a4d85842a9c0d65515f1a40894756.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times [0,1]={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,i],b\\in [0,1]}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(i,0),$ $(i,1),$ and $(0,1).$\n\n![](images/cb/cb530698591dbd71a8058d9faa0c60b636dc654f21e92d65ec8295aeaa67355a.png)\n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the line segment ${0}\\times [0,1]:$\n\n![](images/70/704f8f6f0666d09bb2b8a25eab0548c3eb808e2c9d394d2ae873de35cb0112d1.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389798 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389798 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389798 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389798 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389798 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389798 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389798 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389798 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186389800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389798 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f376ba00-5dab-590e-a791-4441f99a66cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389799 #edb/ref 1080 "images/c8/c87871c50b343792c73fc18dfe92bc2065b18ed3de1e7bb70324b8b43d027206.pn