f 17592186045417] [17592186389916 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181968" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389916 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389916 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S={Z}^{-}\\times N$ in the Cartesian plane?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389916 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6bae802a-d591-53eb-b628-21b012d03cee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389916 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS={Z}^{-}\\times N\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a negative integer and whose $y$-coordinate is a natural number.\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in {Z}^{-},\\,y\\in N}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any natural number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}={(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in N}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/8e/8e6816767cd2010fca1b8991ed9c5e0c42d3a6d6466d78025534bc8362a174b9.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{-2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any natural number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-2}={(-2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in N}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/4d/4d0fe261e790520e6a8786e6f024d5b9cb7cd54c18242103a1f4b77f09653abc.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-5},{S}_{-4},{S}_{-3}$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =…{S}_{-4}\\cup {S}_{-3}\\cup {S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1} \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in {Z}^{-}}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize ${Z}^{-}\\times N$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/f7/f7e54dd973126e3179e79b1ba1a26f4a7c1c541ca764b14c4ccef73b4452509e.png)" #edb/ref 17592