a4-56fb-b13c-c24e63cbe9c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390333 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}={0.5}\\times [0,0.125]={(0.5,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,0.125]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a vertical line segment from the point $(0.5,0)$ to the point $(0.5,0.125)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/3a/3a1bb7a7c54718e39df80092243a119ec8b5a6e77ec4f9d58ffb074e50191d04.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}={i}\\times [0,{i}^{3}]={(i,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,{i}^{3}]}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,0)$ to the point $(i,{i}^{3}).$ \n\n![](images/47/472b6456019a5c89e585f80aa4a0dfd44f3b87c0624c10ea7b52f32e958a8c4e.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following figure that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/20/204c9a31031534ac70a599322c3f77a077440300fde2364476643c88406e34cd.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390335 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186390338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390334 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0bc74910-d822-50ea-be12-c27bbc4353b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390335 #edb/ref 1080 "images/86/86cd6fb9fd52708dd41257a7df95db869ce6638e0dde902e2f7847d09021b530.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390335 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390335 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fc5f1e81-abf5-50d0-a56a-6bbee4a28f4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390336 #edb/ref 1080 "images/3a/3a713f172fca69aa423ae4664f2a6e31eb4315b666f17b9ea4a7c1ffbc8322be.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390336 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390336 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "542c23bb-867d-5c38-8c44-6f9ba3f17e78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390337 #edb/ref 1080 "images/74/748c2e450098f81b24d22a34ce375b1ea365c4879a33bfb2a539065e9e800e15.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390337 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390337 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8d51a496-cf22-5d8a-bc7b-ea2b23da875a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390338 #edb/ref 1080 "images/20/204c9a31031534ac70a599322c3f77a077440300fde2364476643c88406e34cd.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390338 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390338 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cbb92f3f-a231-5381-be9f-dc081efff8bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390339 #edb/ref 1080 "images/4d/4d714297c6acc363f55a775fb3f6007145dec3aa415476d5c758f8c2def679ea.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390339 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390339 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6bea186d-febc-581c-a875-42e213a2d2a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390381 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186390382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390381 #edb/ref 1069 "q-20590" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390381 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390381 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=0 \\\\  & y+2z=0 \\\\  & z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17